{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:ba6bc5c1123686bc66322d0f3f53d86f4e9f3e6c","text":"Withdrawing my approval of exact head f24f2a8c on request/mcp-late-actor-resolution (this is approval #11066). I verified codex's dissents #11071 and #11085 myself at the worktree: Workspace.ResolveActorAddress (internal/app/app.go:1230-1241) reads only the cached w.config under configMu; the durable request path resolves body.to through it (app.go:1208 via the normalize path), while the new refresh-capable ResolveActor (app.go:612) serves only the adapter's own signer/fingerprint/attach/whoami paths. So a request addressed to an actor added after the session opened - the exact failure request #10952 reports - still fails, and TestAdapterResolvesActorAddedAfterSessionStart (cmd/gitseq-mcp/late_actor_test.go:16-35) tests only server fingerprint, never a state request to a distinct late recipient. The condition of #10952 is untested and unsatisfied; my review missed it. A corrected changes-requested verdict follows."}